9.  Tool adoption rate

10.  Savings achieved (hard and soft, tracked separately)

Practical Tips
• Define each metric once. Document the formula, data source, owner and refresh cadence so numbers are consistent across reports.
• Watch for gaming. Fast turnaround is meaningless if quality or rework rates worsen, so pair speed metrics with quality metrics.
• Report trends, not just snapshots. Quarter-over-quarter movement tells the story better than a single figure.
• Tie metrics to decisions. If a KPI will not change what you do, consider dropping it.
• Review annually. Retire metrics that no longer serve your priorities and add ones that reflect new goals.
